{
  "case_id": "2007-07-308",
  "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Jay, is the government running with the fox and chasing with the hounds?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (William M. Jay)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, we think the whole case is in the Title 26 pot, Your Honor, that the whole case should proceed under the provisions of Title 26, meaning that Respondents have already received the full tax refund to which they are entitled. And to be sure, they received interest on that refund. And had they to sue for it, they would have received interest under section 2411. But because they are -- because they are no longer able to proceed under the exclusive tax-refund procedure, of course we think that they -- that they can't plead around that by claiming constitutional damages instead."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But why shouldn't it be a suit contesting the constitutionality? I mean, in the usual case where you seek a refund, there are adjustments that have to be made. But here, if the only question is the constitutionality of the tax, then what is the point of going through any kind of administrative process of the refund route?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Patricia A. Millett)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a question of statutory construction and the problem, as this Court's precedent has made clear in Enochs versus Williams Packing, is that if government -- if the government wants to enjoy the special, extraordinary protections of the tax-refund scheme, it has to assert a plausible basis for tax liability. It hasn't done that here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Nothing different from what it is now, but just Congress makes clear that a tax and alleged violation of the Export Clause falls within the term \"any Internal Revenue tax\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLETT: Then I think my position would be that it does not, because this Court has held for half a century without Congress changing it that any tax means a tax that the government asserts is valid. It doesn't have to be correct. It has to assert that it's valid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why is the Export Clause so, so significant? The only other self-executing constitutional clause that provides for damages automatically that comes to mind is the Takings Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLETT: There -- there's nowhere for them to go for this particular tax. You can't go to tax court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Plus you get interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is the interest the same in amount in either case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, there's nothing there that says you have to have gone through the administrative scheme. All you have to have is an overpayment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT -- the use of any Internal Revenue tax, and your whole argument is this isn't an Internal Revenue tax."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2007-07-308",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81dc6d9f86dcaba9dd9b669ce69dc6048835d86b735a1608a59af4bd70417d9a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81dc6d9f86dc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is that we don't think that a -- an exception to the -- to 7421 should carry over into Section 7422. But even in the circumstances of this case, this is a facially constitutional tax. The tax is imposed on coal mined in the United States."
    },
    {
